lver-type-resolution.md:44 now says the largest API source on antd and shadcn is 75 props, and that Chakra, Mantine and Spectrum are not measured here. It no longer claims evidence from all five corpora.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/ambient.rs:23-25 now states plainly that clause 4 is not part of the production rule: the resolver decides per source through `is_ambient_source`. The note also says clause 4 is kept under cfg(test) only for full-classifier parity.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/ambient.rs:5-8, the test docs at lines 190-196 and the architecture note now name the `measure/layer-only-props` branch and say the classifier and the measurement section are not on this branch yet. A reader is now told where to find them.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/ambient.rs:190-196 now says the data covers antd and shadcn plus synthetic `/p/node_modules/x/index.d.ts` edge cases for the style and DOM-type clauses, and that Chakra, Mantine and Spectrum are not in the data. The overclaim is gone.': 1, 'scripts/collapse_relevance.py:189 now converts source overrides to absolute paths before deriving the root at line 203 and passing paths to the oracle, removing the directory-dependent failure.': 1, "In scripts/collapse_relevance.py:90-129, `check_mode`'s `sys.exit` is now `ran_mode`. `run_lazy` prints a stderr notice and skips only the mode/build cell the bench can't run, so the other cells, including default-mode base-vs-branch lazy times, are still collected and reported.": 1, 'scripts/collapse_relevance.py:182 now makes the work directory absolute before constructing artifact paths, so the oracle can read them after changing directories.': 1, 'scripts/collapse_relevance.py:103 now passes --eager when generating benchmark keys. The eager component_keys path returns published components at crates/core/src/pipeline/watch.rs:466.': 1, '.changeset/collapse-by-relevance.md:8 now reads "An ambient source collapses past 30 props ... Any other dependency source collapses only past 200 props". The contradictory "Only ambient sources collapse now" is gone.': 1, 'scripts/collapse_relevance.py:51-56 `canonical_digest` now only pops `stats`. The dead loop over `durationMs`/`generatedAt` was removed.': 1, 'lazy_bench.rs now echoes `"collapse"` in its JSON line, and scripts/collapse_relevance.py:90-95,115 adds `check_mode`, which fails when the bench didn\'t run the requested mode. A build that ignores the flag can no longer be silently labelled `none`.': 1, '.changeset/linux-x64-runs-on-glibc-2-28.md:2-3 now lists `cargo/caliper-docgen: patch` and `cargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch` alongside the two npm packages.': 1, 'The `# npm and pnpm both read the user-level .npmrc.` comment now sits at callisto-release.yml:497, directly above the `Authenticate with the npm registry` step, below the credentials precheck.': 1, 'callisto-release.yml:275-284: zig legs now run `cargo zigbuild ... --target "${TARGET}.${GLIBC}"` directly, then copy `libcaliper_docgen_napi.so` to `caliper_docgen_napi.${PLATFORM}.node`. napi build no longer gets the suffixed target, so the output name matches what the floor check and the upload expect.': 1, 'scripts/corpora.py:6-7 now says a sparse fetch is enough to extract without dependencies but not for `just bench`, which loads them. bench.py no longer uses sparse corpora.': 1, "docs/measurement.md:110 now says the 1.10×/1.20× thresholds come from a calibration under `--no-cache --no-load-dependencies` that has not been repeated for the addon's configuration. The bench.py docstring says the same.": 1, 'scripts/bench.py:69-72 now uses `corpora.ready(corpus, corpora_dir, sparse=False)`, which needs the `:installed` marker. Without it the script exits and tells you to run `scripts/corpora.py setup`, so dependencies really are loaded.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/callee.rs:61–64 now excludes factory parameters named by supplied arguments, preventing the reported make<T> call from capturing the caller’s module alias. The regression test at crates/core/src/pipeline/tests.rs:4188 covers this case.': 1, 'Commit ef62921 changes every `AtFile { file, inner, .. }` pattern back to `AtFile { file, inner }` in evaluate.rs (e.g. line 42), alias.rs, callee.rs, named.rs, primitives.rs and substitute.rs. The full diff from the base no longer contains any of these churned patterns.': 1, '`CollectedType::AtFile.scope` is now `Option<TypeScope>` (types/collected.rs:174). The wrappers at evaluate.rs:648, chain.rs:202 and evaluate.rs:77 build `scope: None`, and every `AtFile` handler (collected.rs:109, alias.rs:309/940) enters a scope only when one is `Some`, so these wrappers keep the enclosing type parameters.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs:509–520 captures the caller’s scope before entering the interface’s unfilled parameters, then passes it into substitution at lines 540–549. The reported Props<Value> argument now resolves to the module’s number alias.': 1, 'crates/core/src/types/global.rs:63-68: the `in_scope_type_params` field and its "never removed" doc are gone. The new `scope: TypeScope` doc says a declaration\'s own parameters replace the scope while its body is read, which matches `enter_scope`/`leave_scope`.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs:128–135 now registers only unsubstituted parameters, so `Id<Value>` no longer introduces the callee’s `Value` into scope and its argument resolves to `number`. crates/core/src/pipeline/tests.rs:4023–4030 adds exact assertions for that case and its sibling prop.': 1, 'collected.rs:403-404 now prints any key variable that contains a space as `P`, so an opaque `Record<keyof T, V>` displays as `{ [P in keyof T]: V }`. A unit test at collected.rs:1724-1733 covers this.': 1, "named.rs:127-145 now wraps alias expansion in `enter_type_params`/`leave_type_params` (global.rs:263-290), so an alias's parameters stop shadowing once its expansion ends. chain.rs:291-294 adds them only to the `attempt` branch. The new test `an_alias_parameter_shadows_an_outer_alias_only_inside_that_alias` checks that later props using the outer `Value` resolve to `number`.": 1, "Passes at HEAD with the exact repro (interface and type alias variants): a declaration local to a factory no longer loses the factory's parameter, because the factory's parameters sit in ResolveState.closure (callee.rs:60), which entering a declaration does not replace. No UnresolvableImport/severe diagnostic, pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4259.": 1, "Passes at HEAD with the exact repro: interface Box<T> { value: T } + Field<T>(p: { value: Box<T>['value'] }) resolves value to T with no severe diagnostic (pipeline/tests.rs:4129). The cause was that arguments bound without resolver state carried an empty scope; AtFile no longer carries a scope at all (types/collected.rs:167): the writer's type parameters are marked when an argument is bound (resolver/substitute.rs mark_args) and a declaration's unfilled parameters are bound to marked placeholders (bind_declared), so evaluate.rs member and alias reads need no scope. Also checked against TypeScript's checker over 2900 generated programs, 0 mismatches.": 1, "Fixed at HEAD: the made-up Record binder is the first of P, K, Key that the value type does not mention (types/collected.rs, Mapped arm of to_raw_string). Exact repro Box<T, P>(props: Record<keyof T, P>) now composes '{ [K in keyof T]: P }', pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4257 and types/collected.rs a_made_up_key_variable_avoids_the_names_its_value_uses.": 1, "Fixed at HEAD: an alias body is read under its own unfilled parameters only (resolver/named.rs alias arm and expand_alias), never the component's. Exact repro type Value = number; type Saved = Value; Field<Value>(p: { value: Saved }) gives number, pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4198 and, in every resolution order, resolver/tests.rs:3066.": 1, 'The doc comment on `learn()` at dependency_types.rs:806-808 no longer claims it fires only when `write_index` would keep the answer. It says outright that export answers of dropped packages still count, and that the byte compare at line 1303 is what prevents the rewrite. The rule and the guard are now consistent and documented.': 1, 'tests.rs:988-1016 adds `installing_a_package_two_re_export_levels_away_changes_the_warm_answer`, which uses the chain a-kit -> outer-kit -> late-kit and asserts that the warm run sees the newly installed `late` prop.': 1, "dependency_types.rs:1252-1266 now runs a fixpoint that adds every package whose `depends_on` reaches a `with_unresolved` package, then drops their exports with `exports.retain`. So `a-kit`'s negative export rows for `outer-kit -> late-kit` are no longer persisted.": 1, '`packages/storybook/tests/unit/preset.test.ts` no longer has the keys-vs-`OPTION_KEYS` assertion. The test now ends with just `expect(ours?.options).toEqual(options)`.': 1, 'The changeset now promises only that no option can be left out of what goes to the docgen worker. The `option-keys.ts:3-8` doc comment says only `workerOptions` reads the list, and that `provider.ts` and `options.ts` still name their keys by hand. That is the narrower claim the finding offered as a fix.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/evaluate.rs:570–575 now includes a structural hash in the member-read cache key, and crates/core/src/types/collected.rs:290–293 hashes the pinned scope. The generic and module-scope arguments in the reported sequence therefore receive separate cache entries.': 1, 'crates/core/src/pipeline/tests.rs:4123 now asserts `props["first"]` is `{ inner: Value }`. That checks `Wrap`\'s body keeps `Value` as its parameter.': 1, "crates/core/src/types/collected.rs:20 adds the shared constant `MADE_UP_KEY_VARIABLE`. substitute.rs:409 uses it, and the printer at collected.rs:415 now compares `param == MADE_UP_KEY_VARIABLE` instead of `contains(' ')`.": 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/primitives.rs:181-263 now lists `inset*`, `margin/padding` block and inline keys, `outlineWidth`, `letterSpacing`, the longhand border widths and the logical and longhand radii. The comment no longer admits missing keys.': 1, 'crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs:84-85 now recognizes in-scope parameters before looking up module declarations at line 99. The original direct tuple reference therefore remains `Value` instead of expanding the outer alias.': 1, 'At crates/core/src/resolver/primitives.rs:181-183, the comment now says the list is the common subset of csstype `TLength` keys. It names the missing keys (`inset`, `marginInline`, `outlineWidth`, `letterSpacing`, logical and longhand radii) and says `zoom` is listed even though it is not a length. That was one of the two fixes the finding offered.': 1, "Passes at HEAD with the exact repro (type Props = { value: T } local to create<T>, create<string>()): the factory's T stays in ResolveState.closure (callee.rs:60) under every declaration read, so the alias resolves without a warning. Pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4259.": 1, "Passes at HEAD with the exact repro (make<P>(): <C>(p: { value: P; tag?: C }) => ReactElement, make<C>() beside type C = number): value is number and tag is C. The call argument is marked as a declaration and the signature's own C is substituted as a placeholder instead of being put in scope (callee.rs result_props). Pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4277.": 1, 'No longer applies at HEAD: scope is not decided by whether an argument names a factory parameter. make<T, P> called as make<P> over a module type P gives a = number (the argument, marked as a declaration) and b = P (the unfilled factory parameter, a marked placeholder), pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4295; the name-based exclusion in result_chain is gone (callee.rs:57-60).': 1, "Passes at HEAD with the exact repro: type Read<A extends {v: unknown}> = A['v'] with Field<T>(p: { v: Read<{ v: T }> }) (module type T = number too) resolves v to T (pipeline/tests.rs:4156), also in every resolution order (resolver/tests.rs ReadObject in type_parameter_scope_answers_do_not_depend_on_the_order_components_resolve_in). The argument's reference to T is marked when bound (resolver/substitute.rs mark_args), so it needs no AtFile scope through indexed or member reads; the generated-program comparison against TypeScript's checker found 125 such mismatches before and 0 after.": 1, "No longer applies at HEAD: AtFile has no scope field (types/collected.rs:167-171). There is no None-versus-empty-TypeScope distinction left; the writer's type parameters are marked in the argument itself (types/scope.rs mark_placeholder) and TypeScope is only ResolveState.scope.": 1, "Fixed at HEAD: Record<Keys, P> with type P = number prints '{ [K in Keys]: P }', since the binder is a name the value does not mention (types/collected.rs Mapped arm of to_raw_string). Pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4263.": 1, 'Fixed at HEAD: Fixed is read under its own scope, so type Value = \'outer\'; type Fixed = { value: Value }; Field<Value>(p: { fixed: Fixed }) resolves fixed to { value: "outer" }. Pinned by pipeline/tests.rs:4208 and, in every resolution order, resolver/tests.rs:3066 (FixedUse).': 1, "Does not reproduce as written: the tuple element keeps its undefined, so [count?: number] resolves to [number | undefined], not [number]. extractor/mod.rs:945-949 builds Union([T, Undefined]) for the element and resolver/collected.rs:62-80 re-adds the undefined that primitives.rs:17-23 drops from a prop union; pinned by pipeline/tests.rs an_optional_tuple_element_keeps_its_undefined (:4030) and tuple_elements_resolve_whether_plain_labelled_or_optional (:4015). A separate '?' marker needs a per-element flag on PropType::Tuple(Vec<PropType>), which is a wire-format change (types/output.rs:370,657,801,992) and is out of scope here.": 1, 'At `crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs:527` and `:535`, failed explicit named and namespace hops now return `None` immediately, preventing wildcard fallback and the cached incorrect declaration.': 1, '`resolver/mod.rs:782` now reads "Both a missing `typescript` and one lacking a lib file set `diagnostic`."': 1, '`resolver/mod.rs:126-132`: `unresolved_type_help` now returns "\'X\' is a global type, and TypeScript\'s lib files were not found; install typescript…" for unbound names when no lib files exist. `pipeline/tests.rs:347-365` checks that exact help for `Date`.': 1, 'crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs:997–1002 now copies each layer’s panic diagnostics into the flattened loader, preserving earlier errors when the chain is collapsed.': 1, "lazy.rs:655-657 now passes `None` instead of `Some(key)`, so the panic is reported run-wide as in the batch path. lazy_tests.rs adds `a_dependency_loader_panic_is_reported_run_wide_on_every_answer`, which asserts the panic diagnostic in another component's answer has an empty `affects`.": 1, 'crates/cli/src/config.rs:132-133 now says "A path that does not exist is reported first, naming the path the user actually typed", which matches the `!path.exists()` check at lines 134-136. The stale claim about falling back when the file doesn\'t exist is gone.': 1, "crates/cli/src/config.rs:223-228 now resolves both a relative `opts.cache_dir` and a relative `opts.semantic_tsc_path` from the config's folder, so the comment at line 215 is accurate. Tests at tests.rs check `cacheDir`, an absolute `cacheDir`, and `tscPath`, and `.changeset/config-cache-dir-relative.md` documents the change.": 1, 'packages/vite-plugin/src/validate.ts:1-14 no longer has its own `LOG_LEVELS` list. It imports the now-exported `RANK` from diagnostics.ts:11 and checks `Object.hasOwn(RANK, logLevel)`, so the level list is defined in one place.': 1, 'packages/storybook/src/provider.ts:96-123 now uses a `started` flag, so a failure after the first successful `fresh()` warns "could not refresh" instead. Both report flags reset after each success, and provider.test.ts:204-227 covers the refresh warning firing again after a recovery.': 1, "packages/napi/index.js now compares against `require('./package.json').version` in all 54 binding checks. `build:napi` runs scripts/napi-loader-version.mjs to keep it that way after regeneration. scripts/check-packaging.mjs:19-28 rejects any hardcoded version, so a version bump can't make the committed loader stale.": 1, 'docs/storybook-parity.md:40 now cites `packages/storybook/src/options.ts` and `HtmlAttributeMode` in `crates/core/src/types/options.rs`, where `html_attributes: HtmlAttributeMode::Full` is the default.': 1, 'docs/benchmarks.md:133 and :161 now say the recorded bucket counts are not re-derived and do not necessarily add up to the table totals, so the mismatch with 61 and 1,953 is acknowledged instead of hidden.': 1, "docs/benchmarks.md:222 now says RDT and react-docgen ran once each with no spread, matching measurement.md, and that Caliper's cold extraction is timed per fixture above.": 1, 'docs/benchmarks.md:219 now says the WatchSession re-resolve (1.7 to 2.1 ms) and the ensureFresh 3 to 5 ms figures exist, and limits the gap to the end-to-end NAPI ensureFresh call path.': 1, "CONTRIBUTING.md:96 now says the version is pinned in `.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml`, which matches the workflow's `version: callisto@0.17.0`.": 1, 'The comment at weekly.yml:73-75 now says the step "leaves an error annotation", which matches the `::error::` on line 82.': 1, 'weekly.yml:86-92 now passes `--baseline-failed`. weekly.py:595-596 writes a distinct line instead of "No baseline" and adds the failure to issue.md, and the new step at weekly.yml:116-120 fails the job, so `--status success` will not pick this run as the next baseline.': 1, '`crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs:595` now calls `crate::dependency_types::in_node_modules(file.as_str())`, and `in_node_modules` is `pub(crate)` at `dependency_types.rs:1105`. A new test in `resolver/tests.rs` checks that `CollapseInheritedProps::All` leaves backslash `node_modules` paths alone.': 1, 'crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs:454 now calls in_node_modules, whose implementation at lines 1105–1106 recognizes both separators. Windows package declarations therefore no longer get skipped as project files on the reported path.': 1, 'canonical_path.rs:20-52 now checks `needs_verbatim` before stripping. It returns the path unchanged when it is MAX_PATH long or longer, when a component ends in a dot or space, or when a component is a reserved device name (CON/PRN/AUX/NUL/COM1-9/LPT1-9), and tests cover each of these cases.': 1, "At the head, `canonicalize_first_src_dir` (types/options.rs:160), `compute_ambient_global_files` (resolver/mod.rs:631), `governing_tsconfig` (resolver/mod.rs:709), the binding's `on_demand_checker` (binding/src/lib.rs:182) and the CLI's `apply_semantic_backend` (extract.rs:99) all call `canonical_path::canonicalize`. The only raw canonicalize calls left are in tests and examples.": 1, "Fixed by 4b6b234a: needs_verbatim measures the plain spelling (crates/core/src/canonical_path.rs:49-54), so 256-259 char plain paths are stripped, matching discovery's root (discover.rs:24,65,159) and update_file's canonicalize_best_effort (watch.rs:28,500,420). Test the_limit_applies_to_the_plain_spelling_not_the_verbatim_one (canonical_path.rs:105-117) asserts 259-char plain drive and UNC paths are stripped and 260+ keep the prefix.": 1, "The spec text about an echoed message coming first is gone, and the test now parses all of stderr as JSON. Stray git output is suppressed with `run_quiet` in `vcs/access.rs`. Whether the new 'nothing else' wording goes too far is raised as a separate new finding.": 1, 'There is now one function, `format_error_json(command, dry_run, err)`, in `crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs:32`. `main.rs` passes `cli.global.dry_run` to it, and the wrapper that always set `dryRun: false` is gone.': 1, '`crates/callisto-cli/tests/error_envelope_tests.rs` now runs failing `release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest` and `release-pr decide/verify/commit-plan` end to end. It checks `command`, `dryRun` and `error.code`.': 1, "`Command::report_name` in `crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs:81-98` now returns each report's own `Report::COMMAND` (for example `ReleasePlanReport::COMMAND`) instead of a hard-coded string.": 1, "Won't fix: a cosmetic comment-order note at confidence 0.45; the reason is stated one function later and nothing depends on the order.": 1, 'At line 9 of .github/scripts/note-release-pr-rebuild.sh, the `:?` usage message now reads `<success|failure|skipped>`, matching the header comment and the `case`.': 1, '`.github/scripts/release-pr-note.sh:30–34` now explicitly returns on lookup failure, preventing a failed lookup from reaching POST even when errexit is disabled.': 1, '`.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml:222–223` now ru

